<Project>
  <!--
    背景 / Background
    ==================
    中文：NuGet 的 "runtimes/{rid}/native/*" 资源只有在消费方项目声明了
    RuntimeIdentifier（或发布为 self-contained / 单文件）时才会被自动复制到输出目录，
    这是 .NET SDK 的既有行为，不是本包的 bug。为了让"没有指定 RID 的普通
    `dotnet run`/`dotnet build`"（本仓库自己的 Linux 控制台 Demo、以及大多数开发者
    F5 调试 WPF 应用时的典型场景）也能自动拿到正确的原生库，这个文件在**每次构建**时
    根据当前是 Windows 还是 Linux、进程位数是多少，从本包的 runtimes/ 目录里挑一个
    对应的原生库复制到输出目录根。

    English: NuGet's "runtimes/{rid}/native/*" assets are only auto-copied to the
    output directory when the consuming project declares a RuntimeIdentifier (or
    publishes self-contained / as a single file) — this is inherent .NET SDK
    behavior, not a bug in this package. To make plain, non-RID
    `dotnet run`/`dotnet build` (this repo's own Linux console demo, and the common
    case of F5-debugging a WPF app) work out of the box too, this file copies the
    matching native binary from this package's own runtimes/ folder to the output
    directory root on **every build**, based on the current OS and process bitness.

    局限 / Limitations
    ==================
    - 只覆盖 win-x64 / win-x86 / win-arm64 / linux-x64 四个桌面向 RID；Android 不在这里
      处理——.NET for Android 项目请参照 samples/SevenZipLite.MauiDemo 用
      <AndroidNativeLibrary> 显式引入对应 ABI 目录下的 lib7zlite.so（AndroidNativeLibrary
      的 ABI 识别依赖字面目录名，不是这里能通用处理的场景）。
    - 只覆盖“为当前构建机器生成本机可执行”的场景；如果你是交叉发布（例如在 macOS 上
      `dotnet publish -r win-x64`），请显式设置 RuntimeIdentifier，让标准的
      "runtimes/{rid}/native/*" 机制接管，不要依赖这个 .targets 文件按"当前机器"猜测。

    - Only covers the four desktop RIDs win-x64 / win-x86 / win-arm64 / linux-x64;
      Android is intentionally not handled here — for .NET for Android projects, see
      samples/SevenZipLite.MauiDemo and use <AndroidNativeLibrary> to explicitly pull
      in the right lib7zlite.so from its ABI-named directory (AndroidNativeLibrary's
      ABI detection depends on the literal directory name, which this generic
      by-current-OS copy can't replicate).
    - Only applies to "produce a native executable for the machine currently
      building". If you are cross-publishing (e.g. `dotnet publish -r win-x64` from
      macOS), set RuntimeIdentifier explicitly and let the standard
      "runtimes/{rid}/native/*" mechanism take over instead of relying on this file's
      "guess from the current machine" logic.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <_SevenZipLiteNativeRid Condition="'$(_SevenZipLiteNativeRid)' == '' And $([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows')) And '$(PlatformTarget)' == 'x86'">win-x86</_SevenZipLiteNativeRid>
    <_SevenZipLiteNativeRid Condition="'$(_SevenZipLiteNativeRid)' == '' And $([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows')) And '$(PlatformTarget)' == 'ARM64'">win-arm64</_SevenZipLiteNativeRid>
    <_SevenZipLiteNativeRid Condition="'$(_SevenZipLiteNativeRid)' == '' And $([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows')) And '$(PlatformTarget)' == '' And '$(Platform)' == 'x86'">win-x86</_SevenZipLiteNativeRid>
    <_SevenZipLiteNativeRid Condition="'$(_SevenZipLiteNativeRid)' == '' And $([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows'))">win-x64</_SevenZipLiteNativeRid>
    <_SevenZipLiteNativeRid Condition="'$(_SevenZipLiteNativeRid)' == '' And $([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Linux'))">linux-x64</_SevenZipLiteNativeRid>

    <_SevenZipLiteNativeFile Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows'))">7zlite.dll</_SevenZipLiteNativeFile>
    <_SevenZipLiteNativeFile Condition="!$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows'))">lib7zlite.so</_SevenZipLiteNativeFile>

    <_SevenZipLiteNativeSource>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\runtimes\$(_SevenZipLiteNativeRid)\native\$(_SevenZipLiteNativeFile)</_SevenZipLiteNativeSource>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(_SevenZipLiteNativeRid)' != '' And Exists('$(_SevenZipLiteNativeSource)') And '$(RuntimeIdentifier)' == ''">
    <!--
      只在消费方**没有**自己指定 RuntimeIdentifier 时才由这里兜底拷贝——一旦对方指定了
      RuntimeIdentifier，标准的 runtimes/ 解析机制会自己处理，这里重复拷贝反而可能引入
      "两份不同来源但同名"文件互相覆盖的困惑，所以显式避让。

      Only fall back to copying here when the consumer has NOT set a
      RuntimeIdentifier of their own — once they do, the standard runtimes/
      resolution mechanism takes over, and copying here too could confusingly
      overwrite it with a same-named file from a different resolution path, so we
      explicitly step aside.
    -->
    <None Include="$(_SevenZipLiteNativeSource)" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" Link="$(_SevenZipLiteNativeFile)" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
